# Example 14: the three camera movies, and when each one is honest.
#
# SPIN: a full 360 about the vertical axis. Use it for a structure whose
# shape is the point, or as a title loop. It shows every face, and it is
# the only one of the three that is genuinely lossless: nothing is hidden
# at any moment that was not visible a second earlier.
#
# ROCK: a small oscillation, 15 to 25 degrees. Use it to give depth to a
# still panel without the viewer losing their place. A full spin on a
# complicated machine is disorienting; a rock is not. Keep the amplitude
# small enough that the reader never loses the orientation they started
# with, which is the whole reason to prefer it over a spin.
#
# ZOOM: pull in from the whole assembly to one site. Use it to connect an
# overview panel to a zoom panel in a talk, so the audience knows where
# the close-up lives. Always zoom toward something you then label; a zoom
# that lands on nothing is motion for its own sake.
#
# Two rules for all three. Move the camera or the model, never both at
# once, or the viewer cannot tell which. And render at the size you will
# present; scaling a movie up afterwards is visibly soft.
open 4oo8
delete /D-F
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

select /A
open ../../palettes/cas9_domains.cxc
select clear
color /B lab_sgrna
color /C lab_target

view orient
turn y 30
view pad 0.05
windowsize 900 675

2dlabels text "SpCas9  R-loop  4OO8" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.94 size 20 color lab_black bold true

# --- spin: 360 degrees, 180 frames at 30 fps = 6 s ---
2dlabels create mode text "spin" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.88 size 18 color lab_gray bold true
movie record supersample 3 size 900,675
roll y 2 180
wait 180
movie encode spin.mp4 format h264 quality high framerate 30

# --- rock: 20 degrees each way, returning to the start ---
2dlabels change mode text "rock"
movie record supersample 3 size 900,675
# rock N makes the rotation oscillate with a period of N frames
turn y 1 120 rock 60
wait 120
movie encode rock.mp4 format h264 quality high framerate 30

# --- zoom: whole complex in to the HNH domain, then hold ---
# Do not use the zoom command for this. zoom multiplies magnification
# about the current centre, so on a buried target it flies through the
# surface and ends inside the protein looking at backfaces. Instead name
# the two framings you want and let view interpolate between them: the
# camera travels to a composition you have already checked.
2dlabels change mode text "zoom"
view orient
turn y 30
view pad 0.05
view name wide
# pad must be in the same command as the spec. On its own line it
# re-frames every displayed model instead of the selection.
view /A:775-908 pad 0.25
view name close
view wide

movie record supersample 3 size 900,675
wait 20
view close 90
wait 90
2dlabels create site text "HNH nuclease domain" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.82 size 18 color lab_hnh bold true
wait 40
movie encode zoom.mp4 format h264 quality high framerate 30
view wide

# A still from each, for the README
2dlabels change site visibility false
2dlabels change mode text "spin"
view orient
turn y 30
view pad 0.05
cofr frontCenter
save camera_start.png width 2400 supersample 3
